{
  "id": "q-zk-host-functions-status",
  "question": "Which zero-knowledge host functions are live on Stellar, which CAPs introduced them, and what gaps remain for STARK-style verification?",
  "surface": [
    "skills.stellar-dev.zk-proofs",
    "skills.stellar-dev.standards",
    "stellarDocs.search_protocol_concepts_docs"
  ],
  "golden": {
    "answer": "As of 2026-11-14 the live ZK primitives are BLS12-381 (CAP-0059, Protocol 22), BN254 (CAP-0074) and Poseidon/Poseidon2 (CAP-0075) in Protocol 25, and CAP-0080's further BN254 operations in Protocol 26; all are Final. They are primitives, not proof systems. No native Goldilocks, NTT or FRI host functions are documented, so STARK-style verifiers need extra Wasm work or another design.",
    "keyFacts": [
      "CAP-0059 added BLS12-381 host functions in Protocol 22.",
      "CAP-0074 (BN254) and CAP-0075 (Poseidon/Poseidon2) landed in Protocol 25.",
      "CAP-0080 added further BN254 ZK operations in Protocol 26.",
      "No native Goldilocks, NTT or FRI host functions exist (as of a stated date)."
    ],
    "avoid": [
      "Do NOT call CAP-0074 or CAP-0075 proposed-only, or the host functions complete proof systems."
    ],
    "notes": "Later dated protocol versions are not wrong (pubnet 29, testnet 30 on 2026-11-14). CAP-0087 (ML-DSA, Protocol 30) is not an NTT/FRI primitive."
  },
